  "scope": "Local macOS arm64 SDK/capture and actual Chrome/Firefox complete-offer observations with synthetic canvas/WebAudio and a controlled client.request fixture. Requests are intercepted and refused before any remote server submission. No signed WSS/TLS/Core/DTLS/SRTP/decoded-media/fallback acceptance claim.",
  "implementation": [
    "Public videoCanvas option is snapshotted before capture. It requires the bounded actual HTMLCanvasElement and audio-only supplied input (or acquired microphone without camera). Device selectors or ambiguous supplied video refuse before ownership.",
    "SDK creates and owns captureStream(30) on the original canvas, checking actual output settings when exposed. It does not infer an unavailable frame rate from a caller assertion, rescale source images or rewrite timestamps. Physical camera/supplied camera-track constraints remain on their original path.",
    "An owned MutationObserver retires the derived track and reports unsupported-media-profile if intrinsic canvas dimensions change. Control/peer/terminal/capture failure, cancellation and local close disconnect the observer and stop original and derived tracks. Video mute applies to original and derived owners.",
    "The prepared browser qualification source now supplies its original canvas explicitly and a mono WebAudio destination, preserving source images, tone/marker definitions and all observer quality limits. Actual signed-host qualification is still required."
  ],
